 "notes": "Western Addition, sheet 2: solid commercial strips along Fillmore St (x 3080-3124 and 3150-3195) and along Haight St (y 5770-5830), and half blocks split by alleys (Birch, Ivy, Linden, Hickory, Lily, Rose, Laussat), read as streets. Judgment calls: (1) block 841 (3348-3521, 5575-5690) is ONE block with a dead-end alley entering from the east to about (3397, 5640); the thin lines at x about 3417 are lot lines. (2) block 796 (3348-3521, 5012-5128) likewise has a white band from its east side at y about 5065-5072 to x about 3445, read as Birch St's alley entering it, so street. (3) where an alley meets the printed side of a column of half blocks (west ends of Ivy, Linden, Hickory, Lily at x about 3550; Rose at 3742; Laussat at 2955; east ends of Hickory at 3714, Lily at 3912 under OCTAVIA lettering, the 858 alley at 3520) the printed side runs across the alley mouth and joins the two halves; a stroke along the alley's middle separates them. (4) the dimension marks at the Haight St block corners (y 5815-5833) touch the blocks either side; short strokes along the block sides cut them off, so they are street. (5) an ink blob joins 856's south-east corner (3913, 5972) to the angled block below; a stroke at y 5985 splits it, leaving about 20 px of it on 856. Other strokes close small gaps in printed sides (798, 796, 795, 805 and its top, 804, 827, Haight block west side and its FILLMORE lettering on the east side, 842, 852, 860, 831 upper, col at x 3939).",
